    <GaugingStation location="South Wigston" name="Sence" number="28086">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">LaserFlow Index Velocity gauge post-2017. Previously Electromagnetic gauge set in 1:1 formalised banks. Replaces Blaby (28054), daily flow records combined, but not peak flows.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">No bypassing - all flows contained. In 2002 the electromagnetic flows were out by 10% - a new coil/cable was installed in March 2002. Missing data July-December 2016 due to electromagnetic gauge failure. Gauge replaced with LaserFlow index velocity gauge in January 2017.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">LaserFlow ultrasonic gauge under Crow Mill bridge from 2017 onwards. Early record from electromagnetic flow gauge just downstream of bridge.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Flow contained at high flows and fully measured. Early peak flow data are of poor quality, and are therefore rejected. Accuracy of electromagnetic gauge poor from 2006 until replacement in 2017. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in August 2025 (WINFAP Files v14).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Moderately responsive. Substantially augmented by WRW discharges, particularly Wigston.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Moderate to low relief catchment to East and South of Leicester. Mainly Lower Lias (mudstones and limestone) but wholly blanketed by Boulder Clay and alluvium except for headwaters. Urbanised downstream end, otherwise arable and grazing land use.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">EI</Comment>
        </Comments>
